// Verus program: elementwise "isclose" for i8 with a strict (open-interval) tolerance.
//
// Key idea: do all arithmetic comparisons in `int` to avoid i8 overflow.
// `tol` is i8 but required to be strictly positive, so `tol as int > 0`.
// The condition is: -(tol) < (a-b) < tol, i.e. abs(a-b) < tol, but *strictly*.

#![allow(unused_imports)]
use vstd::prelude::*;

